<h1>Preferences - External Software</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>This section allows setting parameters for the command RunExternalSoftware.</p>
<p><img src="Images/Preferences_extsoft.png" width="593px" height="367px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Enable</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Enables the option for loading KUBE file in an external application and adds a start button for the functionality <img src="../User_Interface/Images/Runexternalsw.png" width="31px" height="30px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""> to the toolbar.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Start external software</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Type the fully qualified name of the external software to start or choose its location using the browse button on right.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Add current document to command line</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Check this box if you want to load the current KUBE document in the external software. If the option is not enabled, the external software will start with a blank page.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Save document as</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This field is accessible for editing only when the option "Add current document to command line" is enabled. Type the fully qualified name of the file to load in the external application or choose its name and location using the browse button on right. Possible input data for this field:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>path\name.sab2</i></span>: the current document will be saved in sab2 format and thus loaded in the external software</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>path\name.xxx</i></span>: the current document will be exported to the specified xxx format and then loaded in the external software.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>blank filed</i></span>: if the field is empty, a prompt message will appear when running this command. The user can now choose location, name and type for the file export. When the document is properly saved it will be loaded in the external software.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: If the user types invalid path or location without write permissions, an error message will be displayed and the field will be cleared.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Close document when software is started</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">If this option is selected the current document will be closed in KUBE when the external software is started.</p>
<p class="Note"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: If this option is chosen and the document will be saved in a format other than sab2, then the KUBE software will display a prompt message for saving the current document in sab2 format as well.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Apply button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Press the button to keep the changes made for the command parameters.</p>
